    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **279 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented digits-only telephone storage with normalization applied before the uniqueness check.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Relaxed the `telephone` validation pattern from `^[0-9]*$` to `^[0-9\\s()-]*$` so punctuated input like `(613) 555-0100` is accepted by bean validation instead of being rejected with a 400 before reaching the controller. (This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`'s `@Pattern` at build time.)\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added a `normalizeTelephone(...)` helper that strips every non-digit character (`replaceAll(\"[^0-9]\", \"\")`).\n   - In `addOwner`, the telephone is normalized on the mapped `Owner` **before** the duplicate-telephone check and before persistence, so the digits-only value is what gets stored and returned.\n   - Updated `isDuplicateTelephone` to compare digits-only forms on both sides, so `(613) 555-0100` and `6135550100` collide (409 Conflict).\n   - Applied the same normalization in `updateOwner`.\n\nThe stored/returned `telephone` remains digits-only (still satisfying the entity's `^[0-9]{10}$` constraint), and the new `Cp11Tests` (`coreStoresDigitsOnly`, `functionalityNormalisedDuplicateRejected`) both pass along with all existing tests.",
